## 📌 Project Overview

This repository contains the manual testing documentation for **Mola Mola Diving Center**, a diving and snorkeling website offering activities in Muscat, Oman.

The project focuses on validating website functionality, navigation, booking workflows, input validation, and content presentation through structured manual testing.

- **Website:** https://molamoladivingcenter.com/
- **Developed by:** [Deviora Studio](https://deviorastudio.com/)
- **Manual Testing by:** Ali Mohamed Abdelsalam
- **Testing Date:** October 2026

---

## 🎯 Testing Scope

The manual testing process covered the following areas:

| Testing Area | Coverage |
|---|---|
| Navigation | Website navigation and linked pages |
| Trip & Course Pages | Information, content cards, and visibility |
| Booking | Booking functionality, fields, and pricing summary |
| Forms | Input validation and contact information |
| Packages | Package details and booking selection |
| Gallery | Image and content presentation |
| Responsive Design | Display across different screen sizes |

---

## 📊 Test Execution Summary

A total of **166 manual test cases** were executed.

| Metric | Result |
|:---|---:|
| Total Test Cases | 166 |
| Executed | 166 |
| Passed | 154 |
| Failed | 12 |
| Not Executed | 0 |
| Execution Rate | 100% |
| Pass Rate | 92.77% |
| Fail Rate | 7.23% |
| Bug Report Entries | 12 |

### Execution Status

- 🟢 **Passed:** 154 Test Cases
- 🔴 **Failed:** 12 Test Cases
- ⚪ **Not Executed:** 0 Test Cases

---

## 🐞 Bug Reporting

The bug report documents 12 failed test cases identified during manual execution.

### Key Findings

| Area | Failed Cases | Finding |
|---|---:|---|
| Navigation & Trip Content | 4 | Content obscured by images |
| Contact Information | 2 | Incorrect map/address destinations |
| Booking Form | 2 | Input validation issues |
| Private Trip Pricing | 1 | Pricing behavior requires confirmation |
| Course & Package Booking | 2 | Selected booking options are not preserved |
| Dive Trips Page | 1 | Reported 404; intended URL requires confirmation |

**Note:** Two reported items require further requirement clarification before being confirmed as defects. Some reported failures may share a common root cause.

